WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.764
A brand is the beliefs that predispose people to choose you.

00:00:03.814 --> 00:00:05.485
It matters for five reasons:

00:00:05.535 --> 00:00:06.464
economic engine,

00:00:06.514 --> 00:00:07.702
behavioural shortcut,

00:00:07.752 --> 00:00:09.023
strategy in action,

00:00:09.073 --> 00:00:09.919
culture shaper,

00:00:09.969 --> 00:00:11.698
and volatility moat.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.859
Take two backpacks.

00:00:13.909 --> 00:00:16.489
Louis Vuitton costs about fifteen times more,

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:18.812
with fewer compartments and a worse warranty.

00:00:18.862 --> 00:00:20.275
People still pay.

00:00:20.325 --> 00:00:22.110
That's the brand.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.295
Brands mean margin.

00:00:24.345 --> 00:00:27.514
An iPhone sells for over three times what it costs to make,

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:30.182
a margin above sixty-seven percent.

00:00:30.867 --> 00:00:32.987
Use it like this: argue brand as a commercial asset.

00:00:33.037 --> 00:00:39.321
Attention is cheap, memory is expensive, preference is priceless.
